WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.276 --> 00:00:02.648
- There's a world of
evidence, both scientistic,

00:00:02.648 --> 00:00:03.481
and by scientific--

00:00:03.481 --> 00:00:04.314
- No, no, no, you can't say scientific.

00:00:04.314 --> 00:00:05.147
It's not scientific!

00:00:05.147 --> 00:00:06.205
- There's a world of evidence,

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.096
both hard and anecdotal and by hard--

00:00:08.096 --> 00:00:08.997
- You can't even say hard.

00:00:08.997 --> 00:00:09.830
- I can say hard!

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.865
- It's soft.
- Nah, it's rock hard.

00:00:11.865 --> 00:00:12.698
- It's the softest
evidence there ever was.

00:00:12.698 --> 00:00:14.139
- It's hard as a rock.
- It's see-through.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:16.022
- The evidence I've stated
is it's hard as a rock.

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:18.266
- It's like cellophane, baby!

00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:21.016
(paper rustling)

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:23.403
- Hi.

00:00:23.403 --> 00:00:24.349
I'm Aria.

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:26.335
I'm a production assistant.

00:00:26.335 --> 00:00:29.684
Shane has asked me to read this.

00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:31.697
Welcome to Debatable.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.565
In the interest of a
fair and balanced debate,

00:00:34.565 --> 00:00:37.100
Shane has excused himself
from hosting duties.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.081
He was unable to remain on the sidelines

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:41.331
for this particular outing.

00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:43.970
Are ghosts real?

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.220
It's debatable.

00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:49.201
(triumphant music)

00:00:53.448 --> 00:00:55.448
- [All] Ghosts are real.

00:00:57.499 --> 00:00:58.838
- [All] Nope.

00:00:58.838 --> 00:01:01.597
(intense music)

00:01:01.597 --> 00:01:03.161
- First off, I want to say you've done

00:01:03.161 --> 00:01:05.436
a major disservice to
ghosts by dressing them up

00:01:05.436 --> 00:01:06.986
in this weird Halloween costume.

00:01:06.986 --> 00:01:07.819
- That's ghosts!

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:08.652
That's what you believe in.

00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:09.550
- That's not what ghosts are.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.265
- I hate the word ghost, really

00:01:11.265 --> 00:01:13.181
because it's like, you think of Casper.

00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:14.458
- Yeah, I love Casper.

00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:15.291
He's great.

00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:16.640
He's also a fictional
character in a movie.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.686
- It's so wildly arrogant to think

00:01:18.686 --> 00:01:20.805
that we have it all figured out right now.

00:01:20.805 --> 00:01:23.272
- There's a lot of unexplained
mysteries in the world.

00:01:23.272 --> 00:01:24.366
Ghosts aren't one of them.

00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:26.899
- We have countless stories of people

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:28.733
that we know, trust and love

00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:30.646
who have seen them and felt them.

00:01:30.646 --> 00:01:34.281
- I don't know, trust or love
anyone who has seen a ghost.

00:01:34.281 --> 00:01:36.593
- Look man, I'm not sitting
here trying to say 100 percent.

00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:37.630
- What are you trying to say, then?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.822
- I'm saying--
- You're saying.

00:01:38.822 --> 00:01:39.871
- You never know.

00:01:39.871 --> 00:01:41.108
- There's footage of it.

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:43.169
There's footage of
ghosts caught on camera.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.824
There's footage of things
moving on their own.

00:01:44.824 --> 00:01:46.745
- You guys gotta look
into the YouTube videos.

00:01:46.745 --> 00:01:48.296
I hate the way I sound right now.

00:01:48.296 --> 00:01:51.704
- When I was a kid, there
used to be these two ghosts.

00:01:51.704 --> 00:01:54.827
One was short with a hat
and one was much taller

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:56.040
and they were friends?

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.724
- This sounds a lot
like imaginary friends.

00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:01.389
- We have several EVPs caught on camera.

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:02.534
Those are disembodied voices.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.367
- EVPs are the sound of literally anything

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.957
in a room going (groans).

00:02:06.957 --> 00:02:07.790
- No.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:08.676
- And then Ryan going, oh!

00:02:08.676 --> 00:02:10.332
- What do you sit at your
computer and do all day?

00:02:10.332 --> 00:02:11.165
- I make videos.

00:02:11.165 --> 00:02:12.112
- You manipulate footage?

00:02:12.112 --> 00:02:14.358
- I'm not believing those
YouTube videos either, my man!

00:02:14.358 --> 00:02:15.191
I'm not walking into--

00:02:15.191 --> 00:02:17.104
- You just used a YouTube
video as evidence.

00:02:17.104 --> 00:02:18.703
- It's happened to me a few times, right?

00:02:18.703 --> 00:02:21.071
Where someone has passed
or like an animal.

00:02:21.071 --> 00:02:22.476
Sometimes I would dream of them.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:24.000
- I had a dream about fricking

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.632
being friends with Sara Bareilles.

00:02:25.632 --> 00:02:27.224
I never listen to her music.

00:02:27.224 --> 00:02:29.400
- I could go to any 10
random doors in the world.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.559
About half of them will
say yeah, ghosts are real.

00:02:31.559 --> 00:02:32.408
- Half the people in the world

00:02:32.408 --> 00:02:34.211
think the sun revolves around the earth.

00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:35.752
How many of them just spilled a coffee

00:02:35.752 --> 00:02:36.585
and were like, oh!

00:02:36.585 --> 00:02:38.097
Sammy Davis Jr.'s in my living room!

00:02:38.097 --> 00:02:39.833
- You don't get any sort
of, oh I hope my house

00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:41.934
isn't built on an ancient burial ground.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.522
- I grew up across the
street from a cemetery.

00:02:43.522 --> 00:02:44.806
I was never afraid of it.

00:02:44.806 --> 00:02:45.902
- Baby boy.

00:02:45.902 --> 00:02:48.063
- There's so much evidence
when it comes to scientific--

00:02:48.063 --> 00:02:49.184
- Don't say scientific.

00:02:49.184 --> 00:02:50.017
'Cause it's not scientific.

00:02:50.017 --> 00:02:50.855
- It's scientific if--

00:02:50.855 --> 00:02:52.319
- Have they ever reproduced in a lab?

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:53.202
- I bet you there's a
fair amount of scientists

00:02:53.202 --> 00:02:54.035
who believe in ghosts.

00:02:54.035 --> 00:02:54.954
- I bet you there's not.

00:02:54.954 --> 00:02:56.863
And if it is, it's probably
some fucking horticulturalist

00:02:56.863 --> 00:02:58.727
making green beans in a lab somewhere.

00:02:58.727 --> 00:03:00.748
I don't know anything about the human body

00:03:00.748 --> 00:03:02.159
but I bet ghosts are real!

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:05.491
- No one in their right
mind wants to see a ghost

00:03:05.491 --> 00:03:06.745
unless they're making money--

00:03:06.745 --> 00:03:08.945
- Ryan Bergara wants to see a ghost!

00:03:08.945 --> 00:03:11.464
- I threw a ball down a
hallway that had hundreds,

00:03:11.464 --> 00:03:14.157
literally hundreds of
doorways and windows.

00:03:14.157 --> 00:03:17.420
It lands in a hallway that
has my name painted on it.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.603
How is that possibly not evidence?

00:03:19.603 --> 00:03:21.499
- Your little mind here, it jumps around,

00:03:21.499 --> 00:03:22.725
it connects all the little dots

00:03:22.725 --> 00:03:25.103
in a way that is batshit crazy.

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:25.936
- What?

00:03:25.936 --> 00:03:27.312
- You've been in those
moments where you question it.

00:03:27.312 --> 00:03:29.142
Where it's just like, but what if?

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:31.325
And that's the best part about it.

00:03:31.325 --> 00:03:33.004
The je ne sais que of life.

00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:34.236
Ooh, maybe ghosts are real!

00:03:34.236 --> 00:03:35.811
Ooh, it's fun, whimsy.

00:03:35.811 --> 00:03:38.186
- Have you never walked
into a room and been like,

00:03:38.186 --> 00:03:40.531
ugh, there's something
dark about this place.

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:41.364
- Yeah.

00:03:41.364 --> 00:03:42.218
If there's no lights on.

00:03:42.218 --> 00:03:43.051
Zing!

00:03:43.962 --> 00:03:44.954
- I do think it's fun.

00:03:44.954 --> 00:03:45.787
Halloween's my favorite holiday.

00:03:45.787 --> 00:03:46.620
- Yeah, baby.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.453
That's what's up, dude!

00:03:47.453 --> 00:03:48.286
We're back!

00:03:48.286 --> 00:03:49.119
- But, at the end of the day--

00:03:49.119 --> 00:03:50.194
(they laugh)

00:03:50.194 --> 00:03:51.676
- I think a ghost could come in here,

00:03:51.676 --> 00:03:54.521
pick you up, rock bottom you
into this stupid ghost here

00:03:54.521 --> 00:03:56.817
and you'd still say,
what a weird phenomenon--

00:03:56.817 --> 00:03:59.873
- To be fair, I've asked
them to a thousand times.

00:03:59.873 --> 00:04:01.011
And they've never done it.

00:04:01.011 --> 00:04:02.236
- Yeah, 'cause the
logistics of you are weird.

00:04:02.236 --> 00:04:04.215
You're eight feet tall and well, floppy.

00:04:04.215 --> 00:04:05.507
- Yes, I am floppy.

00:04:05.507 --> 00:04:07.011
But that's neither here nor there.

00:04:07.011 --> 00:04:07.928
- That's kind of here.

00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:10.543
(intense music)

00:04:10.543 --> 00:04:12.255
- You know the difference between

00:04:12.255 --> 00:04:14.455
make-'em-ups in real life, don't ya?

00:04:14.455 --> 00:04:17.496
- The burden of proof lies upon you.

00:04:17.496 --> 00:04:18.546
And you got nothing, buddy.

00:04:18.546 --> 00:04:19.976
- I don't have the facts
and figures in front of me.

00:04:19.976 --> 00:04:23.559
But, how many people
die every Goddamn day.

00:04:24.562 --> 00:04:26.155
- We live in a surveillance state.

00:04:26.155 --> 00:04:29.107
Houses, you set up a little
Nest Cam, you got baby cams.

00:04:29.107 --> 00:04:31.560
Everybody's walking around
with cameras in their pockets.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.880
- Our timelines should be flooded

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.568
with thousands of ghost pics a day.

00:04:34.568 --> 00:04:35.806
We should be tired of 'em!

00:04:35.806 --> 00:04:37.824
We should be saying, too
many ghosts on Instagram.

00:04:37.824 --> 00:04:39.420
There's too many ghosts here.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.555
- You're not gonna find
a picture of a ghost

00:04:40.555 --> 00:04:42.070
on your Outfit of the Day pic.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:46.080
- Those people, though, with
photos of ghosts, you know?

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.136
And they're like, look, it's a face.

00:04:48.136 --> 00:04:51.629
And I'm like, it's a bit
of dust, you fuckface.

00:04:51.629 --> 00:04:53.691
- Every year that goes
on and we don't have

00:04:53.691 --> 00:04:55.849
any sort of video or audio proof,

00:04:55.849 --> 00:04:58.321
the case against ghosts
gets stronger and stronger.

00:04:58.321 --> 00:05:00.585
- The amount of ghosts
that people have seen

00:05:00.585 --> 00:05:05.098
is so small compared to
the amount of people dying.

00:05:05.098 --> 00:05:06.560
- Thank God because we'd all be

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.766
in a constant state of terror.

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:10.408
- Or would we be so used to them

00:05:10.408 --> 00:05:12.905
because they were real and
we were familiar with them

00:05:12.905 --> 00:05:14.107
that we'd just be like, whatever.

00:05:14.107 --> 00:05:14.940
It's a part of life.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:15.773
- Oh yeah, like hey, Johnny!

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:16.606
What's up?

00:05:16.606 --> 00:05:17.439
- Exactly.

00:05:17.439 --> 00:05:18.413
You'd be fist bumping with the ghosts

00:05:18.413 --> 00:05:20.580
but your fist would go
through, 'cause he's a ghost.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.471
- We're not seeing this
influx of ghost proof

00:05:23.471 --> 00:05:25.414
even though it should
be everywhere nowadays.

00:05:25.414 --> 00:05:26.247
- Yeah.

00:05:26.247 --> 00:05:27.080
There could be a ghost here right now.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:27.913
Who knows?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:30.802
- Oh!

00:05:30.802 --> 00:05:33.513
- Look how funny I thought that was.

00:05:33.513 --> 00:05:34.883
- You son of a bitch.

00:05:34.883 --> 00:05:37.720
- You never see a ghost
just hanging out at a party,

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.421
playing pinball, doing fun things

00:05:40.421 --> 00:05:42.076
that they didn't get to do.

00:05:42.076 --> 00:05:44.119
If you came back, why are
you just sitting in a chair?

00:05:44.119 --> 00:05:46.654
Why wouldn't you just be
fricking in Dubai, living it up.

00:05:46.654 --> 00:05:47.543
- They are.

00:05:47.543 --> 00:05:49.289
There's heaps of ghosts in Dubai.

00:05:49.289 --> 00:05:50.621
- Do animals turn into ghosts?

00:05:50.621 --> 00:05:51.454
- Yep.

00:05:51.454 --> 00:05:52.712
They do.

00:05:52.712 --> 00:05:53.872
- Why are you so positive?

00:05:53.872 --> 00:05:55.619
- Because there's been
plenty of sightings.

00:05:55.619 --> 00:05:56.623
- Are there monkey ghosts?

00:05:56.623 --> 00:05:57.490
- Oh, Garrett.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.323
- Are there?

00:05:58.323 --> 00:05:59.156
Yes or no.

00:05:59.156 --> 00:06:00.265
- Dogs, cats, birds.

00:06:00.265 --> 00:06:01.297
- How 'bout toads.

00:06:01.297 --> 00:06:02.130
- Uh, no.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.735
You can really cut out the whole phylums.

00:06:04.735 --> 00:06:05.577
- Trees.

00:06:05.577 --> 00:06:06.720
- Why would there be a ghost tree?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.398
- Why would there be a ghost chipmunk?

00:06:08.398 --> 00:06:10.029
- Because a chipmunk has a soul.

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:11.214
I don't think that's a crazy thing to say.

00:06:11.214 --> 00:06:12.627
Chipmunk probably has a family.

00:06:12.627 --> 00:06:15.039
It has a little wife and
two little chipmunk kids.

00:06:15.039 --> 00:06:16.749
- What the fuck are you talking about?

00:06:16.749 --> 00:06:17.767
- Yeah, it's flawed.

00:06:17.767 --> 00:06:18.600
It's flawed.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.433
It's flawed, baby.

00:06:19.433 --> 00:06:20.266
We all know it.

00:06:20.266 --> 00:06:22.150
You gotta just go with whatever--

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.009
- You're saying?

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:25.573
Whatever nonsense you're
saying, I have to go with it?

00:06:25.573 --> 00:06:26.406
- To a degree.

00:06:26.406 --> 00:06:29.488
(triumphant music)

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:30.321
- Look.

00:06:30.321 --> 00:06:32.332
I respect what Sara has said today.

00:06:32.332 --> 00:06:34.431
All I can do is trust myself and I have

00:06:34.431 --> 00:06:35.589
and they are real.

00:06:35.589 --> 00:06:37.046
A lot of the time, they're not.

00:06:37.046 --> 00:06:38.218
But they are.

00:06:38.218 --> 00:06:39.751
- I think aliens are real.

00:06:39.751 --> 00:06:40.906
- Yeah, me too.

00:06:40.906 --> 00:06:44.579
- The burden of proof falls
upon these nutcases over here.

00:06:44.579 --> 00:06:46.055
- No, I think it's just as much on you

00:06:46.055 --> 00:06:47.704
to prove that ghosts aren't real

00:06:47.704 --> 00:06:49.747
as it is for me to prove
that ghosts are real.

00:06:49.747 --> 00:06:51.132
- The thing is, it's not.

00:06:51.132 --> 00:06:54.767
- Again, say it with me, you never know.

00:06:54.767 --> 00:06:55.767
- I do.

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:57.415
- The arrogance!

00:06:57.415 --> 00:06:59.202
When you start talking
about ghosts, you get mean!

00:06:59.202 --> 00:07:00.591
You get downright mean.

00:07:00.591 --> 00:07:01.424
Look at me!

00:07:01.424 --> 00:07:02.257
You hear me?

00:07:02.257 --> 00:07:03.987
(laughing)
You hear me?

00:07:03.987 --> 00:07:05.210
This is insane.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.127
(triumphant music)

00:07:10.773 --> 00:07:12.857
- You don't get any weird vibes
when you're in a cemetery?

00:07:12.857 --> 00:07:15.940
(speaking gibberish)

00:07:17.315 --> 00:07:18.528
- [Garrett] You can't
just do that every time.

00:07:18.528 --> 00:07:20.386
There should be a Debatable penalty box

00:07:20.386 --> 00:07:21.645
and you're in it, buster.

00:07:21.645 --> 00:07:23.265
Alright?
(sign squeaking)

